  "workarounds": [
    {
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "the electrical table's grey alternates from one parameter to the next, so a parameter keeps one fill over its condition rows: tableStyle.bodyAlternateBackground alternates row by row, and the rows are filled cell by cell with setCellBackground instead"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-34",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "merges go through mergeCells, which marks the covered cells hiddenBy (gotcha merged-cells-hiddenby); the head rows come from parseTSV's headerRows"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-63",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "the register map starts on a page without a page-wide float, and its rows are fitted so the first part runs to the foot of its column instead of keeping room for text"
    },
    {
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "on a closing page a page-wide position 'bottom' float moves up to one float gap under the text (layout.hugClosingFloats, on by default), so page 4 is worded to fill its columns and the outline is drawn 48.3 mm tall: the text above it then ends on a grid line, and the float has no space to move up into"
    }
  ],
